 "method": "City total for New York city (place 3651000), July 1 of each year. 2010-2019 from the 2010-2020 intercensal estimates; 2020-2025 from Vintage 2025. Each series point carries a 'vintage' field naming its file. Borough figures are the Vintage 2025 county estimates for the five counties (Bronx, Kings, New York, Queens, Richmond). Peer cities are the same Vintage 2025 place file.",
 "caveats": [
  "The series joins two Census Bureau products. 2010 through 2019 come from the 2010-2020 intercensal estimates for cities (sub-est2020int.csv), which were revised to agree with the 2010 and 2020 censuses. 2020 through 2025 come from Vintage 2025 (sub-est2025.csv), which starts from the 2020 Census and carries the newest revisions. The two files are not one consistent series; the change from 2019 to 2020 crosses that seam.",
  "Every figure is a July 1 estimate. The intercensal file's April 1, 2020 census population for New York City is 8,804,200; the Vintage 2025 estimates base for that date is 8,805,594.",
  "Vintage 2025 revised every year from 2020 to 2024. Do not compare these numbers with figures from earlier vintages (for example the Vintage 2024 release) without saying so.",
  "Vintage 2024 introduced a revised method for net international migration that raised immigration estimates for 2022-2024 well above earlier vintages; Vintage 2025 population figures include that change."
 ]
}
